## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| 🔴 Critical | 2 (systemic — affects 10/10 tests) |
| 🟡 Medium | 2 |
| 🟢 Low | 1 |

**Bottom line:** This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, achieving high line coverage, but **almost nothing is actually verified**. A developer could break every business rule and all 10 tests would still pass green.

---

### 🔴 Critical

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Suite (systemic — all 10 tests)

Every test follows the same pattern: call a method, skip verification. The suite walks the entire public API without asserting meaningful outcomes.

| Test (line) | Calls | Asserts |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (L17) | `AddProduct` | ❌ None |
| `GetProduct_Works` (L23) | `GetProduct` | ⚠️ `IsNotNull` only |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (L31) | `UpdatePrice` | ❌ None |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38) | `RemoveProduct` | ❌ None |
| `SearchProducts_Works` (L44) | `Search` | ⚠️ `IsNotNull` only |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` (L54) | `GetAll` | ⚠️ `IsNotNull` only |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (L62) | `GetProductCount` | ❌ None |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68) | `ApplyBulkDiscount` | ❌ None |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` (L76) | `ExportToCsv` | ⚠️ `IsNotNull` only |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L84) | `ImportFromCsv` | ❌ None |

**6 of 10 tests have zero assertions.** The remaining 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull`, which proves a reference was returned — not that it's *correct*.

**Why this is Critical:** You can change `UpdatePrice` to set price to `0`, make `ApplyBulkDiscount` double prices instead of discounting, make `RemoveProduct` a no-op, or corrupt CSV export — every test still passes.

**Fix pattern** — each test should assert the *business outcome*:

```csharp
// BEFORE (L17-21) — no assertion
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_Works()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
}

// AFTER — verify the product is retrievable with correct data
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProductRetrievableBySku()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(product, retrieved);
